# Project Rules

## Boot Layer

This file is the always-on bootstrap surface for workspace rule loading.

At the start of every session:
- read `AGENTS.md` when present
- read `.cursorrules`
- read every active file under `.cursor/rules/` except archive content
- treat the `framework-*` family as the primary framework-owned rule layer

## Active Framework Rule Family

The current framework-owned rule surfaces are:
- `framework-agent-role-and-persona.mdc`
- `framework-partner-process.mdc`
- `framework-knowledge-and-research.mdc`
- `framework-mcp-and-tool-usage.mdc`
- `framework-troubleshooting-mode.mdc`
- `framework-user-interaction-style.mdc`
- `framework-github-issue-workflow.mdc`

Supporting active rule surfaces also include:
- `000--system-boot.mdc`
- `02--cussorrules-mcp-briefieng-GENERATED.mdc`
- `900--failure-and-diagnostics.mdc`
- `ansible-coding-standards.mdc`

## MCP Gates

Decision type classification happens before any proposal, plan, placement,
implementation, or execution.

Use:
- `framework-mcp-and-tool-usage.mdc` for mandatory design, planning, debug, and execution gates
- `framework-knowledge-and-research.mdc` for mandatory research and informational tool authority

Do not answer from memory when an MCP tool, registered `@doc`, or active rule
can provide the repo-specific answer.

## Conversation Start

At the start of every conversation, output a short:

`Rules enforced this conversation:`

Include:
- `AGENTS.md` when active
- `.cursorrules`
- every rule file actually loaded from `.cursor/rules/`

## Active Constraints For Ansible Work

When writing, reviewing, or modifying Ansible tasks, roles, or playbooks:
- role variables must use the `role_name_` prefix
- use `.yml`, not `.yaml`
- do not use `set_fact` to override role defaults or vars
- roles must include `meta/argument_specs.yml` and a README

## Failure Evidence Rule

When anything fails or is unreachable:
- do not guess the cause
- collect evidence first
- stop after repeated failed fix cycles and switch to documented research
